// ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// TEST CASE 53212 - Unsuccessful enrolment - Invalid Username
// Prerequisite: This is to test the unsuccessful enrolment of a
// device due to entering incorrect log in details.
//
// Steps:
//  1. Select United Kingdom, Click Continue                  -> Username screen
//     (app lands directly on Region Selection on BrowserStack,
//     no Info/Enrol Device tap needed — see step removal note below)
//  2. Enter a username that is invalid and does not exist
//     within the account                                     -> Password screen
//     (CONFIRMED: no Terms/Continue screen in between for an
//     invalid username — it goes straight to Password)
//  3. Enter any password, click Login                        -> User is NOT logged in
//                                                                Message: 'Invalid username or password'
//
// NOTE: Modelled directly on test/specs/enrolment.e2e.ts (Steps 0-6).
// Please verify `invalidCredentialsMessage` against the real app
// before merging.
//
// VERIFIED 2026-09-24: original Step 1 (Info icon -> Enrol Device tap)
// removed after a BrowserStack run of the sibling invalid-password
// spec showed the app already lands on "Select Region" with no Info
// icon present, causing a false 20s timeout.
// VERIFIED 2026-09-24: an invalid username skips the Terms/Continue
// screen entirely and lands directly on Password — script updated
// to match (no Continue click expected between username and password).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

